{
  "info": {
    "name": "SecurePlan — SCRUM-63 / SCRUM-76: Pruebas Anómalas de Exportación y Errores 500",
    "description": "Colección de peticiones anómalas contra los endpoints de exportación y manejo global de errores del Sprint 3.\n\nCubre todos los casos solicitados en la subtarea SCRUM-76:\n1. Exportar con token inválido o vencido (401 Unauthorized).\n2. Exportar con formato no soportado ?format=xml (400 Bad Request).\n3. Exportar con rango de fechas invertido startDate > endDate (400 Bad Request).\n4. Exportar sin eventos en el rango (200 OK con array vacío o CSV solo con encabezados).\n5. Enviar payload JSON corrupto a un endpoint POST (400 Bad Request con mensaje controlado).\n6. Forzar error 500 de servidor (500 Internal Server Error).\n7. Verificación de que el cuerpo 500 NUNCA filtra stack traces, tablas SQL ni rutas del servidor.\n8. Exportación legítima JSON y CSV con aislamiento entre usuarios.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:3001/api", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token_valido", "value": "{{token_valido}}", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token_invalido", "value": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJmYWtlLWlkIiwiZXhwIjoxNTAwMDAwMDAwfQ.FIRMA_CORRUPTA", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Exportar con token inválido o vencido → 401 Unauthorized",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_invalido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=json",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }]
        },
        "description": "El servidor rechaza tokens con firma inválida o expirados sin revelar detalles internos."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "pm.test('No filtra stack trace ni rutas internas', () => {",
              "  const text = pm.response.text();",
              "  pm.expect(text).not.to.include('stack');",
              "  pm.expect(text).not.to.include('node_modules');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Exportar con formato no soportado (?format=xml) → 400 Bad Request",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=xml",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "xml" }]
        },
        "description": "Solo se permiten los formatos json y csv; cualquier otro formato responde 400 Bad Request."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('Mensaje de validación limpio', () => {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(body.statusCode).to.eql(400);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Exportar con rango de fechas invertido (from > to) → 400 Bad Request",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=json&startDate=2026-12-31&endDate=2026-01-01",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [
            { "key": "format", "value": "json" },
            { "key": "startDate", "value": "2026-12-31" },
            { "key": "endDate", "value": "2026-01-01" }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Si la fecha inicial es posterior a la final, el validador responde 400."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Exportar sin eventos en el rango → 200 OK (vacío controlado)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=json&startDate=1970-01-01&endDate=1970-01-02",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [
            { "key": "format", "value": "json" },
            { "key": "startDate", "value": "1970-01-01" },
            { "key": "endDate", "value": "1970-01-02" }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Si no hay eventos en el rango, devuelve 200 OK con un array vacío [] en JSON o solo cabeceras en CSV."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Devuelve array vacío sin fallar', () => {",
              "  const events = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(events)).to.be.true;",
              "  pm.expect(events.length).to.eql(0);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Enviar payload JSON corrupto a endpoint POST → 400 Bad Request controlado",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"email\": \"invalido@example.com\", \"password\": "
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "Un JSON malformado es interceptado por el filtro global AllExceptionsFilter devolviendo un mensaje 400 sin filtrar trazas de body-parser."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('Mensaje controlado sin traza de body-parser', () => {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(body.statusCode).to.eql(400);",
              "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Cuerpo JSON malformado');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Error 500 inesperado (falla BD o error no controlado) → 500 genérico",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events"]
        },
        "description": "Ante un fallo inesperado del servidor o base de datos, el filtro captura la excepción y responde 500 sin datos internos."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 500 si la BD está inaccesible', () => {",
              "  pm.expect([200, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Si responde 500, no revela datos sensibles', () => {",
              "  if (pm.response.code === 500) {",
              "    const body = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(body.statusCode).to.eql(500);",
              "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Error interno del servidor');",
              "    const text = pm.response.text();",
              "    pm.expect(text).not.to.include('stack');",
              "    pm.expect(text).not.to.include('SELECT');",
              "    pm.expect(text).not.to.include('ECONNREFUSED');",
              "  }",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Inyección SQL en parámetro format → 400 Bad Request",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=json' OR '1'='1",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json' OR '1'='1" }]
        },
        "description": "Caracteres maliciosos en los parámetros de exportación son bloqueados por el DTO y ValidationPipe."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('No contiene errores SQL', () => {",
              "  const body = pm.response.text();",
              "  pm.expect(body).not.to.include('syntax error');",
              "  pm.expect(body).not.to.include('pg_');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Exportación legítima JSON → 200 OK",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=json",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }]
        },
        "description": "Descarga de agenda en JSON con cabeceras correctas."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Content-Type application/json', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json'));",
              "pm.test('Content-Disposition attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Exportación legítima CSV → 200 OK",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token_valido}}" }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/events/export?format=csv",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["events", "export"],
          "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "csv" }]
        },
        "description": "Descarga de agenda en CSV con cabeceras correctas."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Content-Type text/csv', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('text/csv'));",
              "pm.test('Content-Disposition attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('attachment'));"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
